  "dna": {
   "overview": "Iron Man is a slow march built from one melody. The intro is a single open low E bent up from behind the nut: a heavy, sick groan. The main riff slides power chords up B5 – D5 – E5, then shakes G5 – F#5 a half step and falls through D5 home to E5. In the verse the same melody turns into single notes that the vocal sings in unison: B – D – E, then G – F# pull-offs and back home. The bridge drops to the low E string: B, a quarter-bent D, A#, and a chromatic climb A – G# – A – A# back up to B.",
   "rule": "Slide B5 – D5 – E5, shake G5 – F#5, fall through D5 home to E5",
   "law": "Every phrase is the same shape: a rise to E, then a half-step shake above it that falls back home. Slides glue the chords together and the rests leave space, so the riff walks like something heavy. Because the vocal sings the same notes, the guitar line is the song itself.",
